experiment:
Positive control (about 10 min, 0-D). x1, x2 with s = 1 - x1 - x2 and dx_i/dt = s x_i r(x_i), diluted by 2 every cycle. r(x) = k x must give two stable orbits (|delta| -> 1 from random starts); r = k must keep delta/chi fixed.

Main (about 60 min). Copy threads/autopoiesis/worlds/membrane_kinds without its imposed disk conversion; 128^2, 2 seeds, ~20000 t. Arms:
- (A) logistic kinetics, as now.
- (B) superlinear S K_i^2, with decay (F+k) K_i, equal rates, an uncatalysed seed term eps S (eps ~1e-5), and multiplicative noise sigma sqrt(K_i) eta, scanned over 2-3 sigma values.
- (C) B with b1 = 1.2 b2, swapped at T/2 (Matsubara's reversal).

Per cell, log:
- delta = (sum K1 - sum K2)/(sum K1 + sum K2) at birth and at division (the G map);
- parent-daughter kind agreement;
- in-run switches per cell generation;
- conversions of intact cells (L7).

Pass conditions:
- B's G map has stable fixed points near ±1, while A's lies on the identity line;
- >= 90% of daughters are same-kind;
- the switch rate is above 0 and below 0.1 per generation;
- B's kind share stays inside the mirror-arm envelope;
- C's share rises and then reverses after the swap.

If membrane_kinds will not host it, c02's two-kind micelle world (contrib/20261025T1042-c02-micelle-chemoton-2kinds) already has K_i^2 kinetics.
